# LXP Bridge Rust Project Structure

This is a Rust-based bridge application for communicating with LuxPower inverters. The project follows async/await patterns and has a modular architecture.

## Entry Points
- Main binary: [src/main.rs](mdc:src/main.rs) - Entry point with signal handling
- Library: [src/lib.rs](mdc:src/lib.rs) - Core application logic and module organization

## Core Architecture
- **Coordinator**: [src/coordinator/mod.rs](mdc:src/coordinator/mod.rs) - Central orchestrator for inverter and MQTT communication
- **LXP Protocol**: [src/lxp/mod.rs](mdc:src/lxp/mod.rs) - Inverter communication protocol implementation
- **Channels**: [src/channels.rs](mdc:src/channels.rs) - Async communication channels between components
- **MQTT**: [src/mqtt.rs](mdc:src/mqtt.rs) - MQTT client for external communication
- **Home Assistant**: [src/home_assistant.rs](mdc:src/home_assistant.rs) - Home Assistant integration

## Protocol Documentation
**CRITICAL**: The following documentation files contain the complete Modbus protocol specification:
- **[doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md](mdc:doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md)** - Complete Modbus RTU protocol specification
- **[doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md)** - All read/write hold registers (0x03, 0x06, 0x10)
- **[doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md)** - All read-only input registers (0x04)
- **[doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md](mdc:doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md)** - Overview and quick reference guide

## Key Patterns
- Use `anyhow::Result` for error handling
- Async/await with Tokio runtime
- Broadcast channels for inter-component communication
- Command pattern for inverter operations
- Configuration-driven behavior via [src/config.rs](mdc:src/config.rs)

## Dependencies
- **Async Runtime**: Tokio with multi-threaded runtime
- **Serialization**: Serde with YAML/JSON support
- **Networking**: TCP/UDP communication for inverters
- **MQTT**: Rumqttc for MQTT protocol
- **Parsing**: Nom for binary protocol parsing
